{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size","id":861640,"title":"Beasts and Size","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-07T23:35:40-07:00","id":861640,"title":"Beasts and Size","content":"When trying to devise my Beasts Actual Horror I hit a bit of a snag. The Beast I'm designing is a Western Dragon that is more or less based on Smaug from the Hobbit, and when trying to stat out his Size (Specifically, how many points I needed to allot for his Horror form in my Lair) I realized that I don't really have a good Size Chart past Size 7-8, which is roughly a Polar Bear.<br /> <br /> Now obviously a huge Dragon is much bigger than a polar bear, but I can't really find any Rhyme or reason to the size chart that would let me calculate what kind of number a 60 meter dragon might warrant, or even if the system could feasibly support such a thing.<br /> <br /> How would you guys recommend handling this to make it fair? Should I narratively say the dragon is enormous but mechanically has &quot;less&quot; Size than he should? Whats a good place to put him, 10? 12? 25?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:53:48-07:00","id":861647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size#post861640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When trying to devise my Beasts Actual Horror I hit a bit of a snag. The Beast I'm designing is a Western Dragon that is more or less based on Smaug from the Hobbit, and when trying to stat out his Size (Specifically, how many points I needed to allot for his Horror form in my Lair) I realized that I don't really have a good Size Chart past Size 7-8, which is roughly a Polar Bear.<br /> <br /> Now obviously a huge Dragon is much bigger than a polar bear, but I can't really find any Rhyme or reason to the size chart that would let me calculate what kind of number a 60 meter dragon might warrant, or even if the system could feasibly support such a thing.<br /> <br /> How would you guys recommend handling this to make it fair? Should I narratively say the dragon is enormous but mechanically has &amp;quot;less&amp;quot; Size than he should? Whats a good place to put him, 10? 12? 25?</div> </div> </div> </div>About 25 if you're going for a Smaug-type creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:54:49-07:00","id":861648,"title":"","content":"Beasts are Astral symbols. The image doesn't always match the meaning(or the underlying metaphysics) on a one-to-one. So if you just want the image, sure. Make it as big as a skyscraper.<br /> <br /> If you want the metaphysics to match the image, yer gonna have to jack up that Lair by at least four points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:40:29-07:00","id":861740,"title":"","content":"There's a size chart in the CoD corebook, if I remember it correctly size 25 is something like an 18 wheeler, size 100 is a skyscraper. The most effective size a Beast can have with Looming Presence and the Giant merit is 26 at Lair 10, but obviously they can appear larger in the Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:53:23-07:00","id":861796,"title":"","content":"I'd certainly say that the effective size from Looming Presence is very much real on the Horror. You could also say the extra health you get for being Lair 6+ is also represented by getting bigger (although I don't think that would apply to Cyclopean Strength or stuff like that), which puts the Lair 10 maximum at 41 generally, or 51 after satiety expenditure. I don't think spending all 20 bonus points from Lair on size is all that sensible though. You'll probably get more out of it putting it into the attributes. It does of course help the aforementioned Cylopean Strength.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually it might just be 50. I don't thing Giant applies to dream/horror health. Still, this means you can manage 25 size at lair 5. The 20 you'd have in horror form all the time is still fairly respectable too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-08-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:13:48-07:00","id":861885,"title":"","content":"What's the starting size for the horror, size 5 or 6 if you've got the giant merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:26:45-07:00","id":861897,"title":"","content":"Well, it's <i>health</i> is resistance (ok, it says resolve, but resistance makes way more sense) + attribute maximum (ie 5 or lair, whichever is higher) before bonuses. It doesn't really <i>have </i>a definitive size trait as such. I was initially just going with the attribute maximum thing, but then I realised that if you've got giant and no bonus size in Horror form that makes some atavisms weaker, so maybe giant should apply in all forms, even if that doesn't entirely make sense. It just makes everything else less confusing. Plus you paid for it, lets get the bennies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:34:47-07:00","id":861953,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I'd interpret the +attribute maximum as increased Size, at least for the purposes of the Horror, not so much for other dream forms. However, the Dream Form <i>does </i>use your physical Size as the base, so I'd rule that Giant applies in the Lair as well. But would Giant (Advanced) apply? The Beast is treated as bigger the more Satiety it possesses, and in the Lair the Beast can spend Willpower instead of Satiety to active that aspect of Atavisms or Nightmares.<br /> <br /> So, let's take a look at the numbers.<br /> <br /> Size= 5 (With Giant= 6) [With Giant (Advanced) &amp; Satiety 9= 15]<br /> Lair= 10<br /> Looming Presence (with Satiety Expenditure)= 20<br /> Bonuses from Lair= 20<br /> <br /> End Result= 65<br /> <br /> That's... honestly pretty massive. And I don't think that's taking into account the possibility that a Beast Incarnate might be able to count the Size bonus for adopting the Beast-Shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:58:19-07:00","id":861971,"title":"","content":"I'm still not sure how incarnate transformation is supposed to work in the lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:07:24-07:00","id":861979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=861971#post861971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not sure how incarnate transformation is supposed to work in the lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Beast just automatically transforms upon entering the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:32:42-07:00","id":862006,"title":"","content":"You could house rule that your Horror's initial Size is equal to your human form, including the Giant Merit and its Advanced/Epic versions.<br /> <br /> Secondly, you can house rule that you don't have to invest any of your [Lair x 2] dots into the Horror's Size. Each dot of Lair after the first comes with +2 Size for the Horror for free. Therefore, you can distribute your [Lair x 2] dots only among Power/Finesse/Resistance. This stacks with the Normal Effect and Satiety Expenditure of Looming Presence.<br /> <br /> So, following these house rules, a Beast with the Giant Merit, Lair 6, Looming Presence and Satiety Expenditure would have a Horror with an effective AND visual Size of 6 + (5 x 2) + (6 x 2) = 28. That should be enough to imitate Smaug. <br /> <br /> An Incarnate following these house rules could reach the proportions of Cthulhu, which is working as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:38:02-07:00","id":862155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=862006#post862006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could house rule that your Horror's initial Size is equal to your human form, including the Giant Merit and its Advanced/Epic versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I essentially do this and then add 1 for each dot of Lair. But also, my intention was to make it possible for PC Beasts to run into other Beast's Horrors while their both roaming the Primordial Dream. Essentially answering the question of: &quot;what if I merge with my horror and go to feed on someone's nightmare only to find someone else's horror is already feeding on them?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T00:28:54-07:00","id":862497,"title":"","content":"Or you could say how big Horror should be &quot;in real life&quot; and we have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/345029-matter-of-size?p=347750#post347750\">semi working formula for calculating Sizes of things</a> for CoD rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/345029-matter-of-size?p=347750#post347750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a homebrewed version of CthulhuTech using World of Darkness awhile ago. I needed to do Structure calculations for the mecha and decided that for anything that maintains roughly humanoid proportions I'd start with Size 5 for six feet tall and increased Size by 1 for each additional foot of height (so a fifteen foot tall mecha is Size 14). The quick calculation is Size equals Height in feet minus 1. For things that fill more of their cubic volume (like buildings) I flatten it to Size equals Height in feet times 2. It works really well for determining what can and cannot be easily interacted with by mecha of various sizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:11:56-07:00","id":863614,"title":"","content":"I think I'm going crazy, because I'm trying to find where you can increase size for the Horror and I can't. Does anyone mind directing me to the page? I plan on running a Beast game soon and am still going through the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:46:31-07:00","id":863639,"title":"","content":"It's in the &quot;The Horror Itself&quot; sidebar on page 99. And Quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the player gains a pool of points equal to (Lair x 2) to distribute between Power, Finesse, Resistance, <b>and Size</b> as she sees fit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:39:04-07:00","id":863678,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:58:28-07:00","id":863730,"title":"","content":"Just to make sure I followed this right when I read it though. Increasing your horror's size does not give you more health, correct? Spirits health are not based on their size. I guess the main benefit would be increasing their speed and difficulty to push around, correct?<br /> <br /> It still uses spirit rules even when you enter your lair and combine with it, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:09:29-07:00","id":863743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=863730#post863730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to make sure I followed this right when I read it though. Increasing your horror's size does not give you more health, correct? Spirits health are not based on their size. I guess the main benefit would be increasing their speed and difficulty to push around, correct?<br /> <br /> It still uses spirit rules even when you enter your lair and combine with it, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. I'm not entirely sure on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:34:18-07:00","id":863755,"title":"","content":"Hopefully someone can help us understand the difference between a horror by itself and a horror/beast merger that happens when the beast is in their lair. Mainly attributes and health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:35:48-07:00","id":863756,"title":"","content":"A spirit's health is totally based on their size. And also speed is completely unrelated, instead being determined by a species factor.<br /> <br /> Actually thinking about it it would make perfect sense for your bonus dots to get spent on species factor. If your horror is a wolf it should move like one, right?<br /> <br /> Edit because ninja'd: As far as I can tell, the only difference being merged makes to the horror's attributes it that it gets [lair] added to power if it's starving. Heath total likewise stays the same, and the combined form has the wounds of whichever half was in worse state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-11-2016, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T10:57:33-07:00","id":863771,"title":"","content":"Species factor in alot of cases is based off size. Size generally point for point increases health and speed. Page 85 specifies that Magda has a size of 4, 1 str, and 3 dex which equals 8 speed. What caught me off guard when I read how horror stats are determined was the fact size was the same cost as other attributes when it would normally effect two things. Pump all your points into size and you essentially are a optimized normal you with a shat ton of heath which they have no hopes of running from. Fits a Giant though.<br /> <br /> Also, are there maximums that a stat can be for your horror?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 04-11-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:51:17-07:00","id":863799,"title":"","content":"That size = speed thing is annoyingly inconsistent. Only a couple of books mention it in character generation, none of the size-altering merits do, and whether a sample character will follow it seems to be a coin toss. <br /> <br /> Take Boleslav the Giant King, for example. He has strength 8 and dexterity 3, and his speed is given as 17, putting his species factor at 6, which matches his size with no fleet of foot in sight. But he can grow to size 13, and at no point does it mention this affecting his speed at all. Shen Lung, on the other hand, gets a +2 bonus to it when he transforms for reasons I can't really discern. It's not his size, because he grows just as much as his giant counterpart. Species factor, maybe?<br /> <br /> Across other books, there's no indication that shifting affects a werewolf's speed at all, except for the +3 they get from quadrupedal forms, which is spelled out as them shifting to a wolf's species factor of 8. In fact, the species factor of all humans is very clearly set at 5 in that book. No mention of it scaling with size at all.<br /> <br /> So all in all whether the writers intended the size bonus to increase health, speed, or both is rather difficult to determine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:05:42-07:00","id":863811,"title":"","content":"You know what... I always must have missed the size bonuses for werewolf forms because yea, that sort of clearly says size does not effect speed. However, seeing as how they mention a small framed person is speed 4 and giant characters always seemed like the giant merit wasn't worth it if it just added 1 health... I'm going to make a final ruling for my games that Small Framed and Giant merits effect species factor by -1 and +1 respectably. Which makes sense if that is naturally what they are without any outside altering. Temporary size due to forms and whatnot would not grant additional speed, only health.<br /> <br /> Seems like a pretty safe rule to lean on. Anyone else do the same or agree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 04-11-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T21:31:37-07:00","id":864703,"title":"","content":"I use the following rule of thumb. Speed = strength + dexterity + (size \u00d7 pairs of legs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T03:27:36-07:00","id":864799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=864703#post864703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use the following rule of thumb. Speed = strength + dexterity + (size \u00d7 pairs of legs).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that would make a human's Speed factor 10. Which it isn't. And Horrors which appear to be giant spiders would be rediculously fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:16:44-07:00","id":864812,"title":"","content":"<i>Pairs </i>of legs. Humans only have one pair. <br /> <br /> And spiders <i>are</i> really fast for their size, although I don't think the multiple legs play as significant a role in that as the equation would suggest. I think you start to hit diminishing returns after 4. Millipedes aren't known for their speed, are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:28:45-07:00","id":864817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=864799#post864799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> that would make a human's Speed factor 10. Which it isn't. And Horrors which appear to be giant spiders would be rediculously fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that makes it 5. Last I checked I was still a biped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:30:13-07:00","id":864818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=864812#post864812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Pairs </i>of legs. Humans only have one pair. <br /> <br /> And spiders <i>are</i> really fast for their size, although I don't think the multiple legs play as significant a role in that as the equation would suggest. I think you start to hit diminishing returns after 4. Millipedes aren't known for their speed, are they?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, centipedes are freaky fast but size becomes a huge factor. Things smaller than size 1 don't move too far.<br /> <br /> Wolves are faster than humans but not massively so. Horses on the other hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:05:35-07:00","id":864833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=864818#post864818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolves are faster than humans but not massively so. Horses on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe make quick rundown on typical animals to meet and their probable Species Factor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:17:25-07:00","id":864836,"title":"","content":"Well, here's the canon ones from WTF:<br /> <br /> 1 Turtle<br /> 3 Human toddler<br /> 5 Human adult<br /> 8 Wolf<br /> 10 Caribou<br /> 12 Horse<br /> 15 Cheetah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:32:28-07:00","id":864846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/861640-beasts-and-size?p=864817#post864817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that makes it 5. Last I checked I was still a biped.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, my mistake, I read it as 'legs' not 'pairs of legs'. My apologies fro my idiocy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T12:08:20-07:00","id":865048,"title":"","content":"I ended up settling with permanent natural size changes effect speed. This means small frame and giant. It also means increasing size on a horror since I don't see anywhere that suggest you can reallocate those points once you place them. Point for point increasing size would be fairly niche on a horror except for the anakim abilities that rely on being bigger than your opponent. I don't think that horror's need to be as statistically detailed as to allow them to directly modify their speed factor. If they want more speed they can increase any attribute that would offer speed. If they don't want to be bigger to do it they can increase their power or finesse stat. In the end, I think that will be fairly balanced. This also goes well with the idea that changing size temporarily on a werewolf doesn't modify speed except in the case of going to quad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 04-13-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}